    {
      "id": "588a668e371a-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "In a certain code language, 'SUPER' is coded as '61' and 'COLOR' is coded as '77'. How will 'CENTER' be coded in that language?",
      "questionHtml": "In a certain code language, &#39;SUPER&#39; is coded as &#39;61&#39; and &#39;COLOR&#39; is coded as &#39;77&#39;. How will &#39;CENTER&#39; be coded in that language?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "88",
          "html": "88"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "98",
          "html": "98"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "65",
          "html": "65"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "103",
          "html": "103"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage6460ed67aa24ac439fc9ccd7.png\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">The logic followed here is:</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Logic:&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">(Sum of the opposite place value of all numbers) +</span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&nbsp;Number of letter in that word&nbsp;= Code of the word</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&#39;SUPER&#39; is coded as &#39;61&#39;</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Opposite of &#39;SUPER&#39; is &#39;HFKVI&#39;</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&rArr; (8&nbsp;+ 6&nbsp;+ 11&nbsp;+ 22 + 9) + 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&rArr; 56&nbsp;+&nbsp;5&nbsp;= 61.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&#39;COLOR&#39; is coded as &#39;77&#39;</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Opposite of &#39;COLOR&#39; is &#39;XLOLI&#39;</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&rArr; (24&nbsp;+ 12&nbsp;+ 15&nbsp;+ 12 + 9) + 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">&rArr; 72&nbsp;+&nbsp;5&nbsp;= 77.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Similarly, for&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&#39;</span><strong>CENTER</strong><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&#39;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><strong>Opposite of &#39;CENTER&#39; is &#39;XVMGVI&#39;</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><strong>&rArr; (24&nbsp;+ 22&nbsp;+ 13&nbsp;+ 7&nbsp;+ 22 + 9) + 6</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><strong>&rArr; 97&nbsp;+ 6&nbsp;= 103.</strong></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">So, &#39;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">CENTER</span>&#39; will be&nbsp;written&nbsp;as&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&#39;103&#39;</span>.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Hence, the correct answer is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">&quot;Option 4&quot;</span>.</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage6460ed67aa24ac439fc9ccd7.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
